{"uid":"b6dc4436f4a55e4d","name":"test_A5_same_ruling_bound_survives_actual_replan","fullName":"tests.test_ruling_re_park_bound#test_A5_same_ruling_bound_survives_actual_replan","historyId":"e862fb26cb816c17887d3d6d14af8f0b","time":{"start":1791931121692,"stop":1791931121833,"duration":141},"description":"Probe 2 (reconstructed): \"the A.5 bound is per ruling, not per\n    approach.\" Judged RIGHT against `_record_ruling_reparked`'s own\n    docstring (:12082): \"additive... including across a replan that opens\n    a fresh approach -- a ruling's own re-park is spent for the life of\n    the RUN, never reset per approach.\" `rulingReparked` (`status.json`)\n    carries no approach key at all -- unlike `discretionaryGateSpent` and\n    `rejectionSignatures`, both keyed `{\"<approach>\": ...}` and correctly\n    reset by a fresh approach -- so the ruling's exhaustion is the one\n    counter in this family that must NOT reset. This test drives an\n    ACTUAL archive/replan (never a seeded status field) and confirms the\n    SAME ruling, recurring by signature in the FRESH approach, still does\n    not re-park a second time.\n\n    `rejectionSignatures` is cleared before the approach-2 episode purely\n    to isolate this claim from trigger condition 3's own unrelated\n    repeated-signature check (`_repeated_rejection_signature`), which would\n    otherwise intercept first and pause on ITS OWN, different, pauseReason\n    -- never because the ruling bound reset.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Probe 2 (reconstructed): &quot;the A.5 bound is per ruling, not per<br />\napproach.&quot; Judged RIGHT against <code>_record_ruling_reparked</code>'s own<br />\ndocstring (:12082): &quot;additive... including across a replan that opens<br />\na fresh approach -- a ruling's own re-park is spent for the life of<br />\nthe RUN, never reset per approach.&quot; <code>rulingReparked</code> (<code>status.json</code>)<br />\ncarries no approach key at all -- unlike <code>discretionaryGateSpent</code> and<br />\n<code>rejectionSignatures</code>, both keyed <code>{&quot;&lt;approach&gt;&quot;: ...}</code> and correctly<br />\nreset by a fresh approach -- so the ruling's exhaustion is the one<br />\ncounter in this family that must NOT reset. This test drives an<br />\nACTUAL archive/replan (never a seeded status field) and confirms the<br />\nSAME ruling, recurring by signature in the FRESH approach, still does<br />\nnot re-park a second time.</p>\n<pre><code>`rejectionSignatures` is cleared before the approach-2 episode purely\nto isolate this claim from trigger condition 3's own unrelated\nrepeated-signature check (`_repeated_rejection_signature`), which would\notherwise intercept first and pause on ITS OWN, different, pauseReason\n-- never because the ruling bound reset.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791931121659,"stop":1791931121673,"duration":14},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791931121659,"stop":1791931121659,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791931121674,"stop":1791931121683,"duration":9},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791931121674,"stop":1791931121674,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmen